2. Update customer balances in the secondary NoSQL database using MongoDB.
3. Integrate with external APIs for fraud detection and payment processing.
4. Update transaction logs in both relational and non-relational databases using Entity Framework Core.

The method will use optimistic locking to handle concurrent updates, ensuring data consistency across all systems. It will also handle potential network failures and ensure that all updates are idempotent. The trade-off between latency and throughput is optimized for performance and scalability.']

