The class uses a `List<Range>` data structure to store the defined ranges, and provides methods for adding, removing, and updating ranges. It also provides methods for generating random integer or float values within one of the defined ranges. The `Range` class is used to represent each range with its minimum and maximum values.

The class uses a pseudo-random number generator to ensure consistent results across different runs. This ensures that the generated random values are truly random, and not deterministic based on any external factors.']

