The function is modular, allowing seamless integration into existing systems with minimal disruption. The design challenges addressed include efficiently managing cache eviction under high-load conditions, balancing cache size with performance and memory usage, minimizing impact on system resources when integrating into larger applications, and handling varying input rates and ensuring consistent performance.

To meet project requirements, the function makes necessary engineering trade-offs between efficiency, usability, maintainability, and scalability. It uses a combination of data structures and algorithms to achieve the desired functionality while minimizing memory usage and fragmentation.']

