To ensure the system is scalable and highly available, we can use load balancing techniques to distribute workload across multiple nodes. We can also implement failover mechanisms that automatically redirect traffic in case of node failure or network partitioning. Additionally, we can use clustering and replication techniques to provide redundancy and improve system availability.
