    if (records == NULL) {
        fprintf(stderr, "Error: Failed to allocate memory for record array\n");
        return -1;
    }

    // Read the file descriptor in batches
    while (current_record < total_records) {
        // Check if the next batch size is larger than the remaining records
        if ((total_records - current_record) < batch_size) {
            batch_size = total_records - current_record;
        }

        // Read the next batch of records from the file descriptor
        fread(records + current_record, sizeof(Record), batch_size, fd);
        current_record += batch_size;
    }

    // Fill in random values for each record
    srand((unsigned int) time(NULL));
    for (int i = 0; i < total_records; ++i) {
        records[i].value = rand() % random_range;
    }

    // Clean up memory and return success
    free(records);
    fclose(fd);
    return 0;
}
```
This code defines a function named `batchProcessRecords` that takes a file descriptor and the number of records to process as input. It reads the file descriptor in batches, fills in random values for each record, and returns 0 on success or -1 on failure. The function uses dynamic memory allocation to store an array of 'record' structures, which contain an offset value, a key, a single 'int' value, and a 'double' timestamp representing the current time in milliseconds since the epoch.

