Finally, it frees memory for each log entry using `free` and for the report buffer using `free`.

This implementation balances between simplicity and robustness in error handling by providing a simple but flexible approach to handling failures. It also allows for efficient memory management strategies by dynamically allocating memory as needed without causing memory fragmentation or excessive overhead. Additionally, it optimizes for real-time processing by minimizing latency and maximizing throughput, considering the trade-offs between cache performance and memory overhead.']

