To handle potential memory leaks, the code includes a `free_entry` function that frees the memory allocated for an entry when it is removed from the dynamic array. The `realloc` function is also used to free any unused memory at the end of the dynamic array when entries are added or removed. Finally, the `print_all` function includes a `free` call to release all resources when no longer needed.

Overall, this code provides a robust mechanism for managing a dynamic array of `entry` structures, ensuring thread safety, minimizing memory fragmentation, and optimizing cache usage.']

