The code then filters out any log entries with timestamps outside the specified range using a for loop, and allocates memory for an array of filtered log entries and sensor data. Finally, it frees all allocated memory by calling the `cleanup` function.

This is just one way to solve this problem, and there are many other ways to do it. The key is to break down the problem into smaller parts and write code that handles each part effectively.']

