The function then sets up a thread pool to handle data processing using the `pthread` library. The thread pool size is dynamically adjusted based on system load and available resources using a mutex lock and condition variable. The maximum number of threads in the pool is limited by the user-defined `maxThreads` parameter.

The function then creates and starts threads to process data records using the `pthread_create` and `pthread_join` functions. Each thread processes a portion of the input data and free resources once complete using the `pthread_detach` function.

