* `readInputFromStdin()`: This function reads input from standard input and processes it. It uses `fread()` function to read the data from standard input.
* `sigterm_handler()`: This function is called when the program receives SIGTERM signal. It cleans up any resources used by the program and closes the log file.
* `sighup_handler()`: This function is called when the program receives SIGHUP signal. It reads configuration from environment variables and updates the internal configuration of the program. It also prints the new configuration to stdout.

The program uses several libraries such as `stdio.h`, `stdlib.h`, `string.h` and `signal.h` for input/output operations, memory management, string manipulation and signal handling respectively.

