The `LogManager` class uses a linked list data structure to store the log entries. The linked list is protected by a mutex to ensure thread safety. When a new log entry is added or removed, it is first locked by the mutex to prevent other threads from accessing the linked list while the operation is in progress.

The `LogManager` class also provides methods to clear all log entries at once, and to retrieve all log entries as an array. It uses a similar approach to the one used in the previous example, where it locks the mutex before copying the log entries into an array, and then unlocks the mutex after the copy is complete.

This implementation provides thread safety by ensuring that only one thread can access the linked list at any given time. It also allows for efficient addition, removal, and retrieval of log entries, as well as clearing all log entries at once.']

